Join the first ever Danish Zig Day taking place in "nordens paris" Aalborg!
The main focus of the event is to hack on projects together with like-minded enthusiasts. 
Bring your own project or idea, or pair up with someone to work with them for the day.

Anyone is welcome, beginners and long-time ziguanas alike.

# What to expect

Here's the outline:

- *09:30 - 10:00*: Show up, say hi, setup workstations
- *10:00 - 10:30*: present projects or ideas, form groups
- *10:30 - 12:30*: build amazing stuff
- *12:30 - 14:00*: lunch break
- *14:00 - 16:00*: build amazing stuff (continued)
- *16:00 - 17:00*: show others what you made or learned

Please note that you will have to bring/get your own food. (we will probably go get something together).

Bring your own laptop and as we say in denmark "Kom glad!".

# What to work on
Here are some ideas to get your mind going:
- Make your own version of a tool you use
- Make a small game (WASM4 anyone?)
- Make progress on that enourmous side project you have
- Install Zig and run your first program
- Work on software that can benefit your local community
- Contribute to an open source project you care about

# Where is it?

We will meet at **Gasværksvej 46, 9000 Aalborg**. It's a shared office space called "Gassen" and we have the common area for the day.
From Aalborg central station you can take buses 11, 17 or 18 to *Østerport*. From there it is a fresh 15 min. walk.

When you arrive, the door should be open. If not, send me an email. I will let you in.

# How to sign up

Please sign up for the event via email to: herlufba@proton.me

If you can't make the date (or location), but would be interested in participating in a Danish zig day, consider letting me know over email regardless.
I want to make this event work for as many people as possible!
